# Captain
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14Captain = captain's uniform
    .desc = A white KAF dress uniform; the decorations on it were issued in advance, for services to MOKO.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtIS14Captain = captain's uniform skirt
    .desc = A white KAF dress uniform; the decorations on it were issued for services to MOKO.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14CaptainFormal = captain's formal uniform
    .desc = Designed for hosting ceremonies and corporate parties.
ent-ClothingHeadIS14CaptainCap = captain's cap
    .desc = Party-issued property, handed down from captain to captain with everything that comes with it.
ent-ClothingNeckIS14CaptainCloak = captain's cloak
    .desc = A white captain's cloak. In theory it can be used as a parley flag, but whether that is legal is no longer up to the captain.
ent-ClothingHandsIS14CaptainGloves = captain's gloves
    .desc = White fabric, not stained with blood.

# Head of Personnel
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14Hop = head of personnel's suit
    .desc = The pocket sewn into the lining is meant for a flask (not to be confused with the one in the beret).
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14HopFormal = head of personnel's formal suit
    .desc = Meant for backroom talks with MOKO high command.
ent-ClothingHeadIS14HopBeret = head of personnel's beret
    .desc = The pocket sewn under the crown is meant for a spare ID card (not to be confused with the one in the suit).
ent-ClothingHeadIS14HopCap = head of personnel's cap
    .desc = Meant for ceremonial tossing. Its aerodynamic shape lets it fly up to 300 meters in zero gravity.
ent-ClothingNeckIS14HopCloak = head of personnel's cloak
    .desc = In the absence of a flag it can be run up the flagpole.

# Chief Medical Officer
ent-ClothingHeadIS14CmoBeret = chief medical specialist's beret
    .desc = The chief physician's green beret. Its medical-steel cross can break bottles.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14Cmo = chief medical specialist's jumpsuit
    .desc = A specialized jumpsuit for the chief physician. Blood, chemicals, drink stains, crumbs and mayonnaise come off it easily.
ent-ClothingNeckIS14CmoCloak = chief medical specialist's cloak
    .desc = The chief physician's cloak wraps softly around its wearer. Comes with heating for the legs, the torso and the food in the pocket.
ent-ClothingNeckIS14CmoFormalCloak = chief medical specialist's formal cloak
    .desc = Meant for ceremonies and for personally operating on members of the senior party leadership.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14CmoFormalRobe = chief medical specialist's formal robe
    .desc = Meant for personally operating on members of the senior party leadership.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14CmoRobe = chief medical specialist's robe
    .desc = Meant to be worn when visiting operating rooms. May also be worn to show off the rank.

# Research Director
ent-ClothingHeadIS14RdBeret = research director's beret
    .desc = The director's beret, pulled out of an anomaly. Thanks to anomalous exposure it cleans itself, removes dandruff and leaves hair silky.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14RdWhite = white research director's jumpsuit
    .desc = Survives a splash of bleach.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14Rd = research director's jumpsuit
    .desc = Survives a splash of ink.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14RdLabCoat = research director's lab coat
    .desc = Reminds the rest of the staff that he too can run experiments, and even work.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14RdRobe = research director's robe
    .desc = Useless for actual work, worn purely for show.

# Chief Engineer
ent-ClothingHeadIS14CeBeret = chief engineering specialist's beret
    .desc = It is made of cloth, but with that much metal filing in it, it will not pass a metal detector.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14Ce = chief engineering specialist's jumpsuit
    .desc = A jumpsuit for work and for meetings, impossible to set on fire.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14CeWork = chief engineering specialist's work jumpsuit
    .desc = A jumpsuit that withstands high temperature, pressure, heavy mechanical abuse and having industrial spirit spilled on it.
ent-ClothingNeckIS14CeCloak = chief engineering specialist's cloak
    .desc = Made to shield the back from flying production sparks.
ent-ClothingNeckIS14CeFormalCloak = chief engineering specialist's formal cloak
    .desc = Made for ceremonies and for ceremonially cutting the ribbon with an angle grinder.

# Quartermaster (ESO chief)
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14Qm = ESO chief's jumpsuit
    .desc = Engineered so the wearer's chest automatically puffs out.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtIS14Qm = ESO chief's uniform skirt
    .desc = Comes with a built-in bra to raise the morale of the expedition department.
ent-ClothingHeadIS14QmCap = ESO chief's cap
    .desc = Increases damage dealt to the back of the head of anyone who tries to retreat without orders.
ent-ClothingNeckIS14QmCloak = ESO chief's cloak
    .desc = Doubles as a scarf and a pillowcase for the shoulders. In combat it can be raised as a banner.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14QmGreatcoat = ESO chief's greatcoat
    .desc = Keeps you warm in the cold, and in high heat too.
ent-ClothingBeltIS14Qm = ESO chief's belt
    .desc = Fitted with mounts for a holster, a crowbar, a toolbelt and half of the department's property.

# Head of Militia
ent-ClothingHeadIS14HosMilitiaBeret = militia chief's beret
    .desc = Protects the boss's bald spot from draughts.
ent-ClothingHeadIS14HosMilitiaCap = militia department chief's cap
    .desc = Deals -20 to prisoner morale.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14HosMilitia = militia department chief's jumpsuit
    .desc = The militia chief's working uniform. Thanks to the latest SSSP tailoring innovation it fits the wearer and has no size.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtIS14HosMilitia = militia department chief's uniform skirt
    .desc = The militia chief's working uniform.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14HosMilitiaJacket = militia chief's jacket
    .desc = Has a system of inner plates that may, in a pinch, save the wearer from a thrown paper cup.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14HosMilitiaGreatcoat = militia chief's greatcoat
    .desc = Its inner pocket system lets you carry flasks as a form of armor.
ent-ClothingNeckIS14HosMilitiaCloak = militia chief's cloak
    .desc = Sewn by convicts as a token of respect.
ent-ClothingBeltIS14HosMilitia = militia chief's belt
    .desc = Works well as a mount for a holster and a baton, and as a flogging implement.
ent-ClothingShoesIS14HosMilitiaBoots = militia chief's tactical boots
    .desc = The steel toe cap protects your toes from bedside tables and especially tough prisoners.
ent-ClothingHandsIS14HosMilitiaGloves = militia chief's tactical gloves
    .desc = Allow for boxing sessions with prisoners.

# Command secretary
ent-ClothingUniformJumpsuitIS14CommandSecretary = command secretary's suit
    .desc = The official uniform for carrying out the duties of a command secretary.
ent-ClothingUniformJumpskirtIS14CommandSecretary = command secretary's suit skirt
    .desc = The official uniform for carrying out the duties of a command secretary.
ent-ClothingHeadIS14CommandSecretaryCap = secretary's cap
    .desc = Sits gently on the secretary's curls. Designed to be flung off in a fit of passion.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14CommandSecretaryCoat = command secretary's coat
    .desc = Rarely needed during long and hard service, and looks nice draped over the back of a chair.
ent-ClothingOuterIS14CommandSecretaryGreatcoat = command secretary's greatcoat
    .desc = Keeps you warm in low temperatures and doubles as a second blanket.

# Gift set
ent-ClothingHeadIS14HatKnittedOrange = orange (head-worn)
    .desc = By special party permission, at the request of certain high-ranking individuals, approved for wear on the head.
ent-ClothingUnderIS14Tights = tights
    .desc = Sheer woolen tights that build up static in intimate settings.
ent-ClothingShoesIS14DressShoesBlack = dress shoes
    .desc = A special-issue item that adds a few centimeters to the wearer's height. Rated for up to 200 kg.
